    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 disable false\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, the equivalent of Cisco\\'s \"no shutdown\" is \"disable false\" under the interface configuration.\\n- The interface naming convention changes from \"GigabitEthernet1/0/0\" to \"ge-1/0/0\" in Juniper.\\n- Since the command appears on both interfaces (ge-1/0/0 and ge-1/0/1), both translations are included.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 disable false', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 disable false\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, the equivalent of Cisco\\'s \"no shutdown\" is \"disable false\" under the interface configuration.\\n- The interface naming convention changes from \"GigabitEthernet1/0/0\" to \"ge-1/0/0\" in Juniper.\\n- Since the command appears on both interfaces (ge-1/0/0 and ge-1/0/1), both translations are included.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 disable false'}]]": 1,
    "['switchport trunk allowed vlan [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 100', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'The equivalent Juniper configuration command for `switchport trunk allowed vlan 100` would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 100\\n##\\n\\nFor interface `GigabitEthernet1/0/1`, the command would be the same (just changing the interface name):\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would also need additional configuration to set the interface mode as trunk (similar to `switchport mode trunk` in Cisco), which would be:\\n`set interfaces ge-1/0/x unit 0 family ethernet-switching interface-mode trunk`', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 100', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'The equivalent Juniper configuration command for `switchport trunk allowed vlan 100` would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 100\\n##\\n\\nFor interface `GigabitEthernet1/0/1`, the command would be the same (just changing the interface name):\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would also need additional configuration to set the interface mode as trunk (similar to `switchport mode trunk` in Cisco), which would be:\\n`set interfaces ge-1/0/x unit 0 family ethernet-switching interface-mode trunk`', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 100'}]]": 1,
    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/0 disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/0 disable\\ndelete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/1 disable\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the equivalent of Cisco\\'s \"no shutdown\" is to remove the \"disable\" statement from the interface configuration. The Juniper command structure uses \"delete\" to remove configuration elements rather than negating commands with \"no\" as in Cisco.', 'trans_template': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/0 disable'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/1 disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/0 disable\\ndelete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/1 disable\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the equivalent of Cisco\\'s \"no shutdown\" is to remove the \"disable\" statement from the interface configuration. The Juniper command structure uses \"delete\" to remove configuration elements rather than negating commands with \"no\" as in Cisco.', 'trans_template': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/1 disable'}]]": 1,
